# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages. Lives in public/ so `expo export` copies it
# INTO dist/.
#
# WHY the target is /index.html (and not "/"):
#   A rule that rewrites to "/" swallows every static asset too — the font,
#   og-image, robots.txt and sitemap.xml all start returning the HTML shell
#   (verified: Ionicons TTF came back as 1215 bytes of text/html). Pointing at
#   /index.html serves the shell for unknown routes while real files still win.
#
#   wrangler logs a cosmetic "infinite loop detected ... ignored" warning for
#   this rule; it is a false positive from Cloudflare's /index stripping, and
#   the rule is live in production (all routes verified 200 with real files).
/*    /index.html    200